# Environment Variables Template

Copy this file to `.env.local` in your project root and fill in your actual values.
**IMPORTANT:** Never commit `.env.local` to Git. It's already in `.gitignore`.

## Supabase Configuration
# Replace with YOUR new Supabase project's values from Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-id.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key-here

# Server-side only - NEVER expose to frontend
# Get from Supabase Settings → API → Service Role Secret
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

## Stripe Configuration
# Public key - safe to expose in frontend (start with pk_)
# Get from Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API Keys
VITE_STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=pk_test_your_public_key_here

# Secret key - server-side only, NEVER expose to frontend (starts with sk_)
# Get from Stripe Dashboard → Developers → API Keys → Show Secret Key
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_your_secret_key_here

## Optional: Lovable Cloud Auth (if keeping Lovable auth integration)
# Get from your Lovable project settings
# VITE_LOVABLE_PROJECT_ID=your-lovable-project-id

## Development vs Production
# These are read automatically from NODE_ENV:
# - .env.local → used in development (npm run dev)
# - Vercel/Netlify environment variables → used in production

# For Vercel/Netlify, set all the above variables in:
# Vercel: Project Settings → Environment Variables
# Netlify: Site settings → Build & deploy → Environment
